e,"triage":false,"pull":true}},"body":"We came upon this issue today while trying to take a square root of a non-negative series. \r\n\r\nA quick search came up with this old issue: https://github.com/pydata/pandas/issues/2527.The issue was reproduced on 0.15 by tweaking the code from the previous report, which is below:\r\n\r\n```\r\nfrom pandas import date_range, Series\r\ns = Series(index=date_range('1999-02-03','1999-04-05'))\r\ns['1999-02-03'] = 0.00012456\r\ns['1999-02-04'] = 0.0003\r\ns['1999-04-04'] = -0.0\r\ns['1999-04-05'] = -0.0\r\nIn [21]: s.rolling(1).mean()['1999-04-05']\r\nOut[21]: -5.421010862427522e-20\r\n```\r\n\r\nwhich returns -5.4210108624275222e-20.\r\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pandas-dev/pandas/issues/10319/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pandas-dev/pandas/issues/10319/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed"}},"event":"cross-referenced"}]